<title>NETHERLANDS: Wegener completes TV deal.</title>
<headline>Wegener completes TV deal.</headline>
<dateline>APELDOORN, Netherlands 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch publishing group Wegener NV said on Wednesday it had concluded a deal under which Saban Entertainment Inc. of Los Angeles would acquire a &quot;substantial majority stake&quot; in its TV10 television channel.</p>
<p>Wegener gave no financial details of the deal which was first announced in January.</p>
<p>TV10 mainly shows re-runs of popular programmes and can be seen by about 80 percent of Dutch homes linked up to cable distribution networks, though its overall market share is tiny.</p>
<p>Wegener said that as a result of the deal with Saban it would start to screen children's programmes in the morning.</p>
<p>Wegener will retain full ownership of its Dutch music video TV channel The Music Factory (TMF).</p>
